<Layout lang="en" title="About Baitaan: who makes it and how | Baitaan" description="Who makes Baitaan, how each calculator for Mexico is built and checked, and how it stays current.">
  <article class="space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">About Baitaan</h1>
    <p>Baitaan makes free calculators and everyday tools for Mexico, in Spanish and English. They run in your browser, need no account, and follow the country's own law and official tables.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Who makes it</h2>
    <p>Baitaan is built and run by MAAF Studios, a small independent web studio. We write the calculators, the explanations and the worked examples ourselves, and we read every message sent to us.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How each calculator is built</h2>
    <ul class="ms-5 list-disc space-y-1"><li>We start from the law and the official tables: the Ley Federal del Trabajo, the SAT's ISR tariff, the IMSS contribution rates, the UMA published by INEGI and the minimum wages set by CONASAMI. Every page links to the sources it uses.</li><li>We work through real examples by hand and publish them on the page, so you can follow the method and check it.</li><li>Before each release, every formula is recomputed independently against thousands of test cases, and the two must agree to the cent.</li><li>Each page shows the date it was last checked.</li></ul>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How it stays current</h2>
    <p>Mexico's minimum wages and tax tables change on 1 January, and the UMA on 1 February. We update the calculators when the official figures are published, and change the date on each page.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What the results are</h2>
    <p>Estimates made with the official rules. Your employer, the authorities or a court have the final figure, and your contract or a collective agreement can change it. For advice on your own case, <a class="text-link underline" href="https://www.gob.mx/profedet" rel="noopener" target="_blank">PROFEDET, Mexico's federal labor advocacy office, advises workers for free</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Your data</h2>
    <p>The calculators and file tools work inside your browser: nothing you type or upload reaches our server. Read the <a class="text-link underline" href="/en/privacidad/">privacy policy</a> for the details, and the <a class="text-link underline" href="/en/terminos/">terms of use</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How the site is paid for</h2>
    <p>Ads. They never change a result, and we do not sell anyone's data.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Found a mistake?</h2>
    <p>Write to <a class="text-link underline" href="mailto:hello@baitaandessigns.com">hello@baitaandessigns.com</a> with the page, the figures you entered and the result you expected. We check every report, correct the page and update its date. More ways to reach us are on the <a class="text-link underline" href="/en/contacto/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
